 ### Neural Voxel Grids
-Explicit 3D feature grids that replace implicit MLPs for faster optimization. They store learnable features at discrete grid points and use interpolation for continuous queries. Choose when training speed is critical and the scene has a bounded volume. [Link](9326-sparse-and-efficient-representations.md)
+Explicit 3D feature grids that replace implicit MLPs for faster optimization [S1, unofficial]. They store learnable features at discrete grid points and use interpolation for continuous queries [S1, unofficial]. Choose when training speed is critical and the scene has a bounded volume [S1, unofficial]. [Link](9326-sparse-and-efficient-representations.md)
 
 ### Pose Deformation Networks
-Networks that map observation-space coordinates to a canonical space using skeletal priors. They enable the representation of dynamic humans in a static canonical frame. Choose when dealing with articulated subjects like humans. [Link](11366-dynamic-and-deformable-fields.md)
+Networks that map observation-space coordinates to a canonical space using skeletal priors [S1, unofficial]. They enable the representation of dynamic humans in a static canonical frame [S1, unofficial]. Choose when dealing with articulated subjects like humans [S1, unofficial]. [Link](11366-dynamic-and-deformable-fields.md)
 
 ### Generalizable Radiance Fields
-Methods that learn a shared representation across multiple instances (e.g., different humans) to enable fast adaptation to new instances. Choose when you need to render novel instances with minimal per-instance training time. [Link](9273-neural-light-field-representations.md)
